{
  "name": "cartography-set",
  "version": 1,
  "status": "draft",
  "description": "Weights for scoring aws_core against Cartography's own modelled set. Anything Cartography models counts at least 1; the long-established services most accounts rest on (identity, compute, network, storage, encryption, audit, databases) count 5; widely used supporting services and Bedrock count 3. Types outside Cartography's set count 0 unless a rule names them, so this weighting measures parity with Cartography and nothing more. The tiers are a first judgement and unreviewed. The cfn_type rules give the same tiers to the CloudFormation types in the coverage ledger, so the report can say how much of the weighted inventory is collected, decided or still open.",
  "default_weight": 0,
  "rules": [
